ousands separators. A water meter register showing 99,999 m³ (5 digits) — typical. DN600 max 99,999,999 m³ (8 digits). These are register capacities. If instead dots were decimals: 99.999 m³ ≈ 100 m³ for a DN50 — implausible as a register range (DN50 Q3 maybe 40 m³/h → yearly ~ thousands of m³). So thousands separators is right: 99999 etc.\n\nVerification scale intervals: 0,0001 m³ = 0.0001 (1 liter? no, 0.1 L = 100 mL... actually 0.0001 m³ = 0.1 L) fine. Convert commas to dots: 0.0001, 0.001, 0.01, 0.1.\n\nNow assemble JSON.\n\nOrder: certificate, issuing_authority, certified_type, model_family, characteristics, matrix_tables, recommendation, revision_history, footnotes.\n\nJSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"3948757\",\n    \"page_total\": 7,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"M5000\"]\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN50\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN65\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN80\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN100\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN125\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN150\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN200-DN350\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN400-DN500\"},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN600\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"model_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"indicating_range\",\n        \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"model\": \"DN50\", \"value\": 99999},\n          {\"model\": \"DN65\", \"value\": 999999},\n          {\"model\": \"DN80\", \"value\": 999999},\n          {\"model\": \"DN100\", \"value\": 999999},\n          {\"model\": \"DN125\", \"value\": 999999},\n          {\"model\": \"DN150\", \"value\": 999